Original commit body from afa6eea45791ffeb25fbf1ec2a48105f277f45e9:

limits.skipped_passes[].skip_reason_code is renamed to silence_reason --
the name AnalysisRun already uses for the same question on the same closed
axis. SCHEMA_VERSION 0.20.9 -> 0.20.10. Breaking for readers of the old key,
which shipped one version earlier in the same unreleased window.

WHY. Measured on component-model-demo (WI-mamiv): 130 of 162 passes carry
no_candidate_files, 48 on one host and 82 on the other. Which NAME a consumer
had to read was decided by taxonomy.LANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS membership and by
whether the analyzer returns a bare AnalysisResult() or a run with
files_analyzed == 0 -- producer registration and implementation detail, never
a property of the silence.

THE ROUTING IS DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED. Making the HOST a function of the fact
requires an AnalysisRun for the 75 pre-filtered passes, which is exactly what
ADR-0056 'What would change this decision' item 5 reserves to the owner and
judges wrong (ABSENT != EMPTY one level up). What changed is that asking the
question no longer requires knowing which host will answer;
pass_silence.census_silence() is still the union, over the pass CATALOGUE
rather than the two lists.

SCOPE. The serialized key only -- 9 sites. AnalysisResult.skip_reason_code,
the producer-side constructor kwarg, is deliberately NOT renamed: 'skip' is
apt on a skipped result, and test_skip_reason_code_declaration.py gates that
kwarg rather than the output, so it is untouched.

ALSO FIXES WI-gisor, because it is the same spec paragraph. Section 9 claimed
an out-of-taxonomy analyzer finding no files is recorded in skipped_passes
'either way'. Re-measured on canonical dev AFTER the INV-homur pre-filter fix,
since that fix moves profile.languages and could have moved the routing:

    out-of-taxonomy analyzers: 35
      -> analysis_runs : 27   (26 with files_analyzed == 0)
      -> skipped_passes:  8
      -> neither       :  0

'Either way' was never the rule. Taxonomy membership decides pre-filter vs
dispatch; the dispatched ones then split by their own return style. Of the 8
skips, 7 return a bare AnalysisResult() and the 8th is rust_analyzer on the
separate backend-disabled route. The paragraph now names all three routes and
says plainly that a consumer must read both hosts.

ADR-0056 gets a correction note rather than being left prescribing a field
name that no longer exists; its reasoning is untouched, only the name moved.
Three stale references inside CHANGELOG [Unreleased] are reconciled, since
0.20.9 and 0.20.10 land in the same release window.

Full suite 17116 passed, 100% coverage on every changed file, ratchet 667.

